    </header>
    <body>
        <segment id="1" parent="20" relname="span">I'm pleased with the level of thinking going on here on the aspect of intuitiveness.</segment>
        <segment id="2" parent="30" relname="span">Our discussion is definitely geared toward understanding that usability is not only common sense.</segment>
        <segment id="3" parent="32" relname="circumstance">When we begin describing usability in terms of attributes -- intuitiveness, ease of use, learnability and others ---</segment>
        <segment id="4" parent="32" relname="span">we have to be able to link these to concrete measures.</segment>
        <segment id="5" parent="4" relname="otherwise">Otherwise, common sense is our only fall back, which is entirely too vague.</segment>
        <segment id="6" parent="33" relname="span">Comments have also been made in regard to user experience level and intuitiveness.</segment>
        <segment id="7" parent="21" relname="span">This is key to do substantial testing on the novice level</segment>
        <segment id="8" parent="22" relname="span">because so many variables exist in terms of technology experience.</segment>
        <segment id="9" parent="23" relname="span">We cannot lump all users together and assume that one size fits all.</segment>
        <segment id="10" parent="24" relname="span">This is the heart of why we do user testing --</segment>
        <segment id="11" parent="26" relname="antithesis">we design for many concepts concurrently (such as intuitiveness),</segment>
        <segment id="12" parent="26" relname="span">but we must observe how this actually works (or not).</segment>
        <segment id="13" parent="27" relname="span">Without the insight from users, we are drawing our own conclusions.</segment>
        <segment id="14" parent="29" relname="span">(Most people in this class are highly skilled in technology.</segment>
        <segment id="15" parent="14" relname="elaboration">It's natural for us to "forget" what being a novice user "feels" like.</segment>
        <segment id="16" parent="29" relname="elaboration">We have to observe others to recall the difficulties.)</segment>
        <segment id="17" parent="19" relname="summary">It makes me proud to see so many fine HCI advocates in this class!</segment>
        <group id="18" type="span"/>
        <group id="19" type="span" parent="18" relname="span"/>
        <group id="20" type="span" parent="19" relname="span"/>
        <group id="21" type="span" parent="6" relname="elaboration"/>
        <group id="22" type="span" parent="7" relname="nonvolitional-cause"/>
        <group id="23" type="span" parent="8" relname="elaboration"/>
        <group id="24" type="span" parent="9" relname="elaboration"/>
        <group id="25" type="span" parent="10" relname="elaboration"/>
        <group id="26" type="span" parent="25" relname="span"/>
        <group id="27" type="span" parent="12" relname="elaboration"/>
        <group id="28" type="span" parent="13" relname="elaboration"/>
